From b7c3a62ff5e35f5746f5361733408483bea6c7d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:38:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Playable calculation: reuse the simulation, skip no-op
 trigger scans

Three behaviour-preserving performance changes (pin 348b37db):

* PlayerImpl.getManaAvailable/getPlayable: reuse the game when it is already a
  playable-calculation simulation (inCheckPlayableState) instead of copying it
  again. The flag is only ever set by GameImpl.createSimulationForPlayableCalc.
* TriggeredAbilities.checkTriggers: skip the trigger-list copy when no trigger
  matches the event type. All 1325 checkEventType implementations in the tree
  are side-effect-free type tests (static scan); the integrity checks that would
  notice the skipped processingDone calls are disabled and only toggleable by
  editing the source.
* AbilitiesImpl.singleton: single-element Abilities without a varargs array.

Deliberately NOT included (measured to change behaviour):
* GameState.getPlayersInRange fast path for RangeOfInfluence.ALL: inRange is a
  per-turn snapshot that excludes players who left in earlier turns; the fast
  path re-includes them (seed 10 of the 4-player pod: 4406 vs 4327 decisions,
  different winner).
* CardImpl.getAbilities(Game) returning the live list: ShayCormacEffect and the
  Room cards remove abilities while streaming that list
  (ConcurrentModificationException, 20 errors in RoomCardTest/ShayCormacTest).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
